&lt;h2&gt;About Motivity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Motivity, we&#39;re a mission-driven team of clinicians, researchers, and engineers dedicated to improving outcomes for individuals who receive data-driven services such as Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA).&amp;nbsp; Our platform streamlines everything from clinical data collection to practice management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Motivity is looking for an HR Manager to own and run our people operations day to day. You will be the go-to person for employees and managers on payroll, benefits, hiring, onboarding, and HR compliance, and you will make sure the fundamentals happen accurately, on time, and with care that supports and builds upon our culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone who is just as comfortable processing a payroll change as they are running a review cycle. You will partner closely with leadership, and help keep the employee experience warm, consistent, and well documented.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Payroll and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare payroll and process changes (new hires, terminations, raises, bonuses, PTO) in JustWorks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enroll new hires in benefits, administer open enrollment, and answer employee questions about pay, benefits, and time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track PTO and keep payroll and benefits records accurate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Operations and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain employee files, policies, and handbook. Keep records organized and audit-ready&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor state payroll and employment requirements and resolve filing issues, escalating as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the contractor classification intake and escalate decisions as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage the virtual mailbox and route mail appropriately.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage our ATS, Greenhouse&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full hiring lifecycle supporting Hiring Managers and operate as a key part of the hiring process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend offers, send contracts, and manage pre-boarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Onboarding and Offboarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run orientation and integration for new employees and contractors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and launch an expanded Orientation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage workflows related to both onboarding &amp;amp; offboarding including new hire check in process and exit interview procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate system access with IT at the start and end of employment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Management &amp;amp; Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run performance reviews in Google and support the calibration process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run engagement and integration surveys, then synthesize and share the results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compensation cycles and communicate decisions through clear channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture and Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan recognition (birthdays, anniversaries, Motivator of the Month) and culture events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support MotivNation, our ERG, and the ongoing integration of our India Team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Manager of Culture of our India Team; some overlap with the IST timezone will be necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in HR Operations or Generalist roles, ideally at a SaaS company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on payroll and benefits administration in a PEO or HRIS such as JustWorks, with awareness of multi-state compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running a clean offer and onboarding process in an ATS (Greenhouse preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a remote or hybrid organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort running performance review, survey, and compensation cycles, and presenting the findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization, attention to detail, and the discipline to document what you do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and discretion with confidential information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A service mindset with employees and managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus Points For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to or experience in Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA), and or Organizational Behavior Management (OBM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to international or contractor employment (India is a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting an acquisition or integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing HR records for an audit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and be a part of a company that is making a real difference. We&#39;re a growing, mission-driven startup and this is your chance to get on board. As part of our talented and driven international team, you&#39;ll enjoy the flexibility of a fully remote company, working from wherever you&#39;re most comfortable. We support our team with competitive benefits, including comprehensive health care, a 401k plan, parental leave, and an open time-off policy, because we believe in taking care of our employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that specific benefits may vary depending on your country or region. We do not offer visa sponsorship for this position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected range for this position is $115,000 - $130,000. Our salary data is based on internal and external benchmarking. The final offer will vary based on assessment of a candidate&#39;s skills and experience, and our budget for the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Marketing Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Motivity is looking for a Product Marketing Manager to own how our product is positioned, launched, and sold across a wide market, from solo BCBA-owned practices to national operators with 50+ locations and a formal procurement process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is our first dedicated product marketing hire. The role spans positioning and messaging, launch strategy, enablement, competitive intelligence, and customer insight, working closely with product, sales, and marketing to better communicate our unique approach and value we bring to the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person for this role is a strong writer who can turn a complex, regulated product into a sentence a busy clinic owner understands on the first read. They are comfortable owning scope and ambiguity, and they build positioning from direct customer conversations rather than from a spreadsheet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Positioning and messaging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own how Motivity is positioned across a wide range of buyers — from a solo BCBA owner with three learners to a national operator with 50+ locations. Turn what our product does into what it means for a Clinical Director versus a CFO versus the RBT using it in session.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the category narrative for our move upmarket so enterprise buyers can answer questions about multi-site governance, audit readiness, and migration at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launches and go-to-market&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product launch strategy and execution end to end: the brief, the narrative, the sequencing, the channels, and the post-launch read on whether any of it worked. Turn the roadmap into external stories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the customer-facing changelog and the plain-language product source of truth that everything else (campaign copy, customer-facing decks, website, release comms) draws from.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the assets that move deals: one-pagers, pitch decks, demo scripts, solution briefs, competitive battlecards, talk tracks, and proof points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and align with Sales and Product through internal launch training that makes sure what Sales says matches what Marketing publishes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the competitive picture in ABA software and turn it into something our team can use. Our competitors range from entrenched all-in-one incumbents to point solutions for data collection and billing, and displacement conversations are a large share of how we win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate where competitors are heading, not just where they are. Sharpen our differentiation accordingly, including the honest version: where we&#39;re genuinely better, and where we need to acknowledge a gap and reframe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer and market insight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the working ICP and persona documentation that Sales prospects against and Marketing targets against, and keep it current (and usable) as the market moves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with RevOps to run win/loss analysis and feed the patterns back into messaging, campaign strategy, and the roadmap. Identify which customers are seeing outsized results and worth building a story around.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5+ years in product marketing at a B2B SaaS/technology company, with launches you can walk us through: what you positioned, how you enabled the field, and what actually changed as a result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing. Much of this job is turning something complicated into a sentence a busy clinic owner understands on the first read.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working with AI tools to improve processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort owning ambiguity and sequencing your own work, as you’ll be the first person doing this job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine interest in a domain with real regulatory and clinical weight (payer requirements, authorization utilization, documentation compliance, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The instinct to talk to customers directly and often, rather than positioning from a spreadsheet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare, behavioral health, ABA or autism services, EdTech, or another regulated, clinically-driven market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a BCBA, RBT, or have worked in or adjacent to ABA service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with Product and Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to both SMB and enterprise buyers within the same product, and the judgment to know those are not the same motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive or displacement-heavy market experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
